== FINDINGS FOR THE LEAD (not FAILs) ==
F1 (against required mutation (d)): the mutation the brief mandates be killed is
provably an equivalent mutant — byte-identical rendering, demonstrated above. No
test can satisfy that requirement; the requirement, not the work, is at fault.
F2 (residual, criterion 2): "only for !Qualifies" is guarded twice — once in the
handler (`!c.Qualifies`) and once in the template (`{{if $c.Qualifies}}` first
branch) — and each masks the other, so breaking BOTH simultaneously (my variant
d') is caught by no test. I could not construct a reachable input where that
combination renders wrong wording, so I do not treat it as a defect; if the lead
wants it closed, the cheap fix is a render-level test that a qualifying row with
PlanDesignBelowTarget=true and PlanFloor set still reads "Meets target".
F3 (environment, not GV3): /tmp/budget2-gv-final-snap was deleted and its path
reused by another agent during this verification. Any later checker pointed at
that path will be verifying the wrong tree.
